    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d593">

                <pb facs="0820" n="750" sameAs="frus:frus1862/pg750"/>

                <head>Mr. Corwin to Mr. Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 28.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States of
                                America,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1862-06-28"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 28, 1862</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Nothing has occurred since my last
                    despatches to change in any important particular the aspect of affairs in
                    Mexico. The French still occupy their place at Orizaba. The guerillas cut off
                    their communications from Vera Cruz as far as Puebla.</p>
                <p>I enclose copies of a correspondence between the captain of a rebel regiment on
                    the frontier of Texas and the Mexican authorities.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>THOS. CORWIN.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State of the United States, Washington,
                            D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>






